{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And it shall be, the place…</b> Build for yourselves the Temple of Choice in Jerusalem. And so it says of David: ״וַיְהִי כִּי יָשַׁב הַמֶּלֶךְ בְּבֵיתוֹ וַה׳ הֵנִיחַ לוֹ מִסָּבִיב מִכָּל אוֹיְבָיו וַיֹּאמֶר הַמֶּלֶךְ אֶל נָתָן הַנָּבִיא רְאֵה אָנֹכִי יוֹשֵׁב בְּבֵית אֲרָזִים וַאֲרוֹן הָאֱלֹהִים יֹשֵׁב בְּתוֹךְ הַיְרִיעָה״ (II Samuel 7)." "<b>There you shall bring…</b> Above it is stated regarding Shiloh, and here it is stated regarding Jerusalem. Therefore Scripture divided them, to permit [use of] the high places between one and the other: from when Shiloh was destroyed and they came to Nov, and Nov was destroyed and they came to Giv'on — the high places were permitted until they came to Jerusalem (Zevachim 119)." "<b>The choice of your vows.</b> This teaches that he must bring from the choicest (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:46.380523630Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}